    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ACT 2 \u2014 Clips arrive on your phone\n\n**No polling, no Wait-node loop.** OpenShorts calls this webhook once per job (success **and** failure, so nothing ever hangs). Each finished 9:16 clip lands in your Telegram with two buttons: \u2705 publish or \u274c skip \u2014 a human approves every post, which is also what keeps you on the right side of YouTube's inauthentic-content policy.\n\n**Setup**: copy the **production** URL of the *Clips ready* webhook node and paste it as `webhook_url` inside *Start OpenShorts job*. Telegram fetches videos by URL up to ~20 MB; bigger clips fall back to a message with the download link and the same buttons.",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 400,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "note-act2",
      "name": "Act 2 note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -560,
        340
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "openshorts-machine-clips",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "clips-webhook",
      "name": "Clips ready (webhook)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -80,
        440
      ],
      "webhookId": "30f3bc66-1f03-4d2f-94b8-aed49571238d"
    },
    {
