    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ACT 3 \u2014 Tap \u2705, it gets scheduled\n\nThe Telegram trigger listens for the approval buttons. Every approved clip is scheduled through OpenShorts (which posts to every social account you connected there) at a rate of **one post per day**: approve five clips today and you just filled five days of content.\n\nThe next free slot is computed from the **queue the server actually holds** (`GET /api/social/scheduled`), not from a counter inside n8n \u2014 two clips approved seconds apart would otherwise both book the same slot and go out together.\n\n**Setup**: none beyond the Telegram credential \u2014 the chat id comes from the button tap itself. Change the platforms list in *Schedule social post* if you want fewer networks.",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 400,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "note-act3",
      "name": "Act 3 note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -560,
        800
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "updates": [
          "callback_query"
        ],
        "additionalFields": {}
      },
      "id": "tg-trigger",
      "name": "Approval buttons",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.telegramTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        -80,
        900
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "telegramApi": {
          "name": "Telegram bot"
        }
      },
      "webhookId": "906a710d-3e76-4911-b7e6-f336e6da5d66"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const cb = $json.callback_query || {};\nconst [action, jobId, clipIndex] = String(cb.data || '').split('|');\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    action: action || 'skip',\n    job_id: jobId || '',\n    clip_index: parseInt(clipIndex || '0', 10),\n    chat_id: cb.message && cb.message.chat ? cb.message.chat.id : null,\n    clip_title: cb.message ? (cb.message.caption || '') : '',\n  },\n}];"
      },
      "id": "parse-button",
      "name": "Parse button",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        140,
        900
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "c2",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.action }}",
              "rightValue": "pub",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "if-approved",
      "name": "Approved?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        360,
        900
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// One post per day, derived from the queue the server actually holds.\n// Workflow static data was the obvious place to remember the last slot, but\n// two approvals tapped seconds apart run as two executions that both read the\n// old value and book the SAME slot. The scheduled list is shared state, so\n// counting it cannot race with itself in that way.\nconst queue = $input.first().json.scheduled_posts || [];\nconst item = $('Parse button').first().json;\nconst DAY = 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000;\nconst taken = queue\n  .map((p) => Date.parse(p.scheduled_date))\n  .filter((t) => !Number.isNaN(t))\n  .sort((a, b) => a - b);\nlet slot = Date.now() + 10 * 60 * 1000;  // never schedule in the past\nfor (const t of taken) {\n  if (Math.abs(t - slot) < DAY) slot = t + DAY;\n}\nreturn [{ json: { ...item, scheduled_date: new Date(slot).toISOString() } }];"
      },
      "id": "reserve-slot",
      "name": "Pick next free slot",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        800,
        840
      ]
    },
